0 -> [Aren't fructose sweetener and corn syrup the same thing?]
Fructose sweetener and corn syrup are not the same thing, although they are related. Corn syrup is a thick, sticky liquid made from corn starch. It contains a mixture of sugars, including glucose and fructose. High-fructose corn syrup (HFCS) is a specific type of corn syrup that has been processed to have a higher concentration of fructose.

Fructose sweetener, on the other hand, specifically refers to the sugar fructose itself, which is a simple sugar found naturally in fruits and honey. While HFCS contains fructose, it also contains glucose and other components, making it different from pure fructose sweetener.

