1 -> [What does OGL denote?]
The term "OGL" in the context of the document refers to "Other Government Licenses." This term is used in the discussion about the legal domestic cigarette industry in India. The document mentions that the industry is "faced with the high level of taxes on the legal domestic cigarette industry, incentivises illegal flow of cigarettes" and that "the OGL (Other Government Licenses) system is a complex and cumbersome process."

The OGL system in India is a regulatory framework that governs the production, sale, and distribution of tobacco products. It involves obtaining various licenses from different government agencies, which can be a lengthy and costly process for manufacturers and retailers. This complexity and the associated costs are part of the challenges faced by the legal domestic cigarette industry, contributing to the attractiveness of illegal cigarette flows and tax arbitrage opportunities.

