The mechanism used to lift the insert out of the shell involves the AB extractor. Specifically, the three tips of the AB extractor are placed into any three scallops on the face of the Pinnacle shell. When the extraction handle is lightly tapped one to three times, the resulting vibration releases the taper of the Ultamet insert and the Pinnacle shell. This causes the shell to be lifted out of the mechanism by the designed release mechanism, as illustrated in Figure 4. This process ensures that the insert is effectively and safely removed from the shell.

3 -> [In performance data, what is the % honor for medicine?]
5.0

