0 -> [In which year Old Age assistance program was established?]
The Old Age Assistance program was established in 1935. This program was designed to provide financial assistance to individuals who were aged 65 or older, or those who were blind or disabled, regardless of age. The initiative aimed to ensure that these individuals could meet their basic needs and maintain a decent standard of living. Over time, this program evolved into the more comprehensive Supplemental Security Income (SSI) program, which continues to offer support to eligible individuals.

1 -> [Which age range of persons are eligible for Old Age assistance program?]
The Old Age Assistance program is available to individuals who are 65 years of age or older. This includes those who are currently 65 or have reached that age in the future. Additionally, the program also assists those who are unable to earn a living, regardless of their age, as long as they meet other eligibility criteria such as being a resident of the county and having limited income and resources.

