0 -> [How the Capital expenditure on Research & Development is shown based on section(H)?]
The capital expenditure on Research & Development is shown as a deduction from the profit & loss account in the year it is incurred. The amount is then credited to the profit & loss account. Any gratuity for the year is calculated by the Life Insurance Corporation and is credited to fixed assets under the Group Gratuity Scheme, as applicable.

