0 -> [Aren't fructose sweetener and corn syrup the same thing?]
No, fructose sweetener and corn syrup are not the same thing. Corn syrup is a thick, sticky liquid made from corn starch, primarily used as a sweetener and humectant in food products. It contains mostly dextrose (glucose) and smaller amounts of other sugars.

Fructose sweetener, on the other hand, is derived from corn but is specifically processed to isolate fructose, which is sweeter than sucrose (table sugar). High-fructose corn syrup (HFCS) is a common form of fructose sweetener, often used as a cost-effective alternative to sugar in various food and beverage products. It typically contains a mixture of fructose and glucose.

