3 -> [What type of information should EPA use to identify conditions of use for inclusion in scoping?]
EPA should use high quality, best available information to identify conditions of use for inclusion in scoping. This includes information from credible sources such as reporting already made to EPA or other credible sources of public information, as well as information of varying quality, integrity, credibility, and reliability available on the internet, social media, and online journals. The EPA should apply its Quality System to information collected and evaluated to ensure it has conducted a data assessment to verify that the information is of sufficient quantity and adequate quality for their intended use.

