0 -> [What is on the Y (vertical) axis?]
The Y (vertical) axis represents the percentage of production. It is labeled with values ranging from 0 to 60, in increments of 10. This axis shows the proportion of total production that is being measured at different stages.

To elaborate further:

- The Y-axis is labeled "Percentage production."
- The values on the Y-axis start from 0 at the bottom and go up to 60 at the top.
- The increments are marked at every 10 units (0, 10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60).

This axis is used to track how the percentage of production changes over time, as indicated by the different lines representing various stages or conditions (Pretest, Interim, etc.).

