Sodium plays a crucial role in regulating water balance in the human body. It helps maintain the proper balance of fluids by controlling the movement of water in and out of cells. Sodium attracts water, so when sodium levels are high, more water is retained in the bloodstream, and when sodium levels are low, water is excreted. This balance is essential for maintaining blood pressure, nerve function, and overall cellular health.

