0 -> [Aren't fructose sweetener and corn syrup the same thing?]
No, fructose sweetener and corn syrup are not the same thing. Fructose sweetener is a sweetener made from corn during a wet milling process, and it is chemically identical to the fructose found in fruits and honey. On the other hand, corn syrup is a sweetener that is a byproduct of corn starch processing and contains dextrose and other sugars. It is not a low-calorie sweetener like fructose sweetener.

